# component: context-menu
# decisions: A11Y-13, API-19, BRD-1, DOC-1, DOC-2, FRM-4, INT-1, OVL-13
# hunks:
#   OVL-13: the same two hosts `dropdown-menu` has — `ContextMenuContent`'s own portal is scoped
#     on its Positioner, and the exported `ContextMenuPortal` scopes a `display: contents` wrapper.
#   INT-1: `cursor-default` is removed from the item, the submenu trigger, the checkbox item and
#     the radio item.
#   FRM-4: `data-disabled:pointer-events-none` is dropped from the item, the checkbox item and
#     the radio item, so a disabled row stays hoverable.
#   BRD-1: `ContextMenuContent` draws a real 1px `border border-border` instead of upstream's
#     `ring-1 ring-foreground/10` box-shadow outline (MK reversed BRD-1 to ours, 23-09-2026). A
#     border survives forced colours and matches `foundations/elevation`; nothing else moves.
#   A11Y-13: the destructive `ContextMenuItem`'s focused ink `focus:text-destructive` becomes
#     `focus:text-destructive-text`. Upstream paints the fill as ink on its own `/10` tint
#     (3.99:1 in light, under the AA floor); the family's `-text` ink clears it. The resting ink
#     measures 4.77:1 light and 6.21:1 dark on the popup (`contrast.browser.test.tsx`,
#     menu-destructive-rest), over the floor, so it and the icon ink stay upstream's.
#   API-19: `ContextMenuItem`, `ContextMenuCheckboxItem` and `ContextMenuRadioItem` each call
#     Item's `useItemDescriptionId()`, provide its `register` through `ItemDescriptionContext`,
#     and set `aria-describedby` on the row once an `ItemDescription` inside it registers. A
#     two-line row (`ItemContent` > `ItemTitle` + `ItemDescription`) therefore reads its second
#     line as the row's accessible description, which is where a disabled row carries its reason.
#     A one-line row renders no `aria-describedby`. Imports `ItemDescriptionContext` and
#     `useItemDescriptionId` from `@/components/ui/item`.
#   cn: `import { cn } from "cn"` becomes `@vegastack/design` — our npm layer owns `cn` (DOC-2).
#   formatting: prettier reflow plus the `registry-stamp.mjs` provenance header (DOC-1); no
#               decision of their own.
